title: Genesis 6 – The Days of Noah
description: A study in Genesis 6: man’s wickedness, God’s judgment, and grace found by faith.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-6-the-days-of-noah.html

=== Introduction
--- The Days of Noah [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 6
sub: Man’s wickedness, God’s judgment, and grace found by faith.
refs: Genesis 6:1-9
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

--- Only a short while after creation
lead: Genesis 6 is not far removed from the garden. Adding the ages given in Genesis 5, the whole world before the Flood fits inside a few overlapping lifetimes.
tile: 930 | Adam dies. Noah’s father Lamech is already 56.
tile: 1056 | Noah is born.
tile: 1656 | Methuselah dies, at 969.
tile: 1656 | The Flood, in Noah’s 600th year.
note: Years counted from creation by the ages in Genesis 5 and 7.
refs: Genesis 5:27; Genesis 7:6
p: Men who had heard of Eden from Adam’s own mouth were alive when Noah’s father was born. And still, within ten generations, mankind had fallen so utterly that it corrupted the earth itself.

--- The pattern of salvation
lead: The story of the patriarchs from Adam to Noah is a pattern of salvation given to us by God. Man has always been saved by grace through faith.
big: Hebrews 11:7
panel: Noah walked as Enoch walked | “Enoch walked with God.” “Noah walked with God.” A just man, perfect in his generations, who found grace in the eyes of the {Lord}. [[Genesis 5:22]] [[Genesis 6:8-9|Genesis 6:8–9]]
panel: Grace, then and now | “For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God.” [[Ephesians 2:8-9|Eph 2:8–9]]

=== Before the Flood
--- When men began to multiply
scripture: Genesis 6:1-3
- The sons of God chose wives by sight: “that they were fair.” Not by faith, but by what pleased the eye.
- The {Lord} said His Spirit would not always strive with man, “for that he also is flesh.”
- To limit the wickedness of man, God set his days at an hundred and twenty years, and man’s natural life began to shorten.
callout-honest: **Who are the sons of God?** This study reads them as believers, those who “call upon the name of the {Lord}.” Faithful believers differ here, and we cover both views in depth in [[lesson:genesis-6-sons-of-god|Genesis 6 – Sons of God]]. [[Genesis 4:25-26|Gen 4:26]] [[John 1:12]]

--- Giants in the earth
big: Genesis 6:4 | mark: men which were of old; men of renown
panel: Giants were already there | “In those days,” before the text describes the unions. And “also after that.”
panel: The children were men | Mighty men of renown. Of great stature, no doubt, as we see in Goliath and his people, and even occasionally today. [[1 Samuel 17:4]] [[Numbers 13:33]]
center: The genetic potential of man is what it is, divinely made.

=== Man’s wickedness
--- Only evil continually
big: Genesis 6:5 | mark: man
center: This is God’s judgment of man. He tells us it was the wickedness of man that caused Him to repent of our creation.

--- It repented the Lord
heading: It repented the {Lord}
scripture: Genesis 6:6-8
- God repents, turning in His dealings given the outcome, and it grieves Him at His heart.
- He resolves to destroy man, and with him beast, creeping thing, and fowl, for the earth too had become corrupt.
- But Noah found grace in the eyes of the {Lord}.

--- The generations of Noah
big: Genesis 6:9-10
p: This is the prologue to the generations of Noah. God sets out to destroy His creation, but for the sake of one just man, Noah, He offers grace and gives a path to salvation, for Noah and his house: his wife, his three sons, and their wives. [[Genesis 6:18]]

--- The earth filled with violence
scripture: Genesis 6:11-13
panel-warn: Blood cries from the ground | As we saw in the murder of Abel, the earth itself is corrupted by our sin and the spilling of innocent blood. [[Genesis 4:10-11|Gen 4:10–11]]
panel-warn: Blood defiles the land | This is established Biblical doctrine. Nations fall by this very thing, and here all the earth has been made corrupt by man. [[Numbers 35:33]]

--- It is man that has fallen
lead: The story of the Flood is clear throughout: it is man’s own wickedness that God is punishing. Humanity has fallen. Man is corrupt and wicked of heart, the same then as it is today.
scripture: Romans 3:10
scripture: Romans 3:23
p: Only Noah stayed faithful, God’s Spirit striving with him, but not so with the rest of mankind.

=== The doctrine
--- Evil is not something foreign
lead: Many false doctrines place evil as something “other”: introduced by bloodlines, genetics, or ancestry, with salvation only for a certain people, chosen by nothing but their genes. Genesis 6 shows that it is man’s own wickedness that destroys us.
scripture: Acts 17:26
panel-warn: If man is lost by his genes | then he is condemned by a god of bloodlines, not the God of the Bible.
panel-warn: If man is saved by a quality given him | then he has no free will to receive or reject Christ.
panel-warn: If man is judged for another’s sin | then he has no soul liberty to be saved by his own faith in Christ.
refs: Ezekiel 18:20; John 3:16; Romans 10:13
center: We are all one blood: given to the same temptations of the flesh, the same sinful nature, the same free will, and the same need for salvation.

--- The oldest excuse
scripture: Genesis 3:12
p: Since the garden, Adam blaming his sin on Eve and on God for creating her, man has looked for an excuse to justify himself before the {Lord}: push it off on the devil for offering temptation, or place it on the sins of another.
callout: Blame the flood on the demonic lineage of half-human chimeras, and we are really saying, “Maybe it’s not our fault, God.” But God knows our heart, and He says the thoughts of man’s heart were only evil continually. [[Jeremiah 17:9-10|Jer 17:9–10]] [[James 1:14]]

--- Why this matters for salvation
lead: This understanding is the basis for faith in God for salvation: the knowledge that we are wicked and sinful creatures, deserving death and Hell, and in need of saving.
big: Romans 6:23
p: To walk with God, to strive with His Spirit, requires His grace and His promise of salvation. Not of ourselves, but as a gift of God. [[Ephesians 2:8-9|Eph 2:8–9]]

=== Grace and the ark
--- God’s plan of salvation: the ark
scripture: Genesis 6:14-16
stat: 300 | cubits long, about 450 feet
stat: 50 | cubits wide, about 75 feet
stat: 30 | cubits high, about 45 feet
note: Cubits taken as about eighteen inches. God gave Noah the size, the material, the type, and the purpose: one ark, one door.

--- “With thee will I establish my covenant”
scripture: Genesis 6:17-21
p: Judgment and salvation come in the same breath. The same God who brings the Flood makes a covenant to preserve the ones who come into the ark: “wherein few, that is, eight souls were saved by water.” [[1 Peter 3:18-21|1 Pet 3:20]]

--- Thus did Noah [title]
overline: Genesis 6:22
big: Genesis 6:22
p: Faith obeys. Noah, warned of things not seen as yet, built what God told him to build, the way God told him to build it. [[Genesis 6:22]] [[Hebrews 11:7]]

--- A figure of baptism
lead: The Flood cleansed the earth of its wickedness in a global baptism, itself a picture of the death, burial, and resurrection of Christ.
scripture: 1 Peter 3:21
scripture: Romans 6:4
refs: 1 Peter 3:18-21
center: The waters that judged the world bore up the ark. Those in it passed through death into a new world.

=== As the days of Noah
--- As the days of Noah were
big: Matthew 24:37
refs: Matthew 24:37-39
- Eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage: things continue as ever. Man is just as caught up in the things of this world.
- Like Noah, we who are obedient to the Gospel follow God’s instructions to our salvation, mindful of the times we are in.
- So we keep watch of the skies for His return in glory. [[Matthew 24:42]] [[Matthew 24:44]] [[Titus 2:13]]

=== Close
--- Grace through faith [title]
overline: Genesis 6:8
heading: Noah found grace
sub: in the eyes of the {Lord}.
point: Sin is the problem | Our nature in the flesh, in a fallen world, chooses sin and rejects the word of God. God judged that wickedness, not something foreign to man.
point: Grace is the answer | Then and now, man is saved by grace through faith.
point: Obedience is the evidence | Thus did Noah, according to all that God commanded him.
point: Watch | As the days of Noah were, so shall the coming of the Son of man be.
